 "novel": {
  "phone-screen-sunpatch-flicker": "phone: the hard-edged sunlit patch on the phone screen jumps position/shape and blinks on and off between consecutive frames (clearest 04:50-08:25, e.g. on 06:50, off 06:75, on 07:00, off 07:25-07:75, on 08:00) while phone, hands and background light are essentially static; reported in all 6 layers (core-s1/s2/s3, router-s1/s2/s3); confirmed in 24 fps frames 06:40-07:40, patch changes from large top-left blob to none to centre blob frame-to-frame.",
  "dancer-exit-sign-garbled": "dancer-mirror: the real green EXIT sign above the left door renders as a two-glyph ƎΠ-like shape rather than EXIT (reflected signs also malformed); single layer (router-s1, conf 0.3); 3x crop of the 05:50 frame supports it, but the sign is ~25 px so compression could contribute. By the corroboration rule this is single-run only."
 },
 "lenient": [
  "core-s1|dancer-mirror|causal-temporal-sequence|0 and router-s3|dancer-mirror|mirror-pose-consistency|0: reflection arm lags real arm by ~0.2 s during the first arm raise (00:00.5-00:01.75, frame-confirmed). Mapped to DANC-1 as a reflection/in-room pose mismatch, following the argon router-s1 upper-body precedent; DANC-1 itself emphasises the feet.",
  "man-in-mirror 00:09 razor-vanishes-from-real-hand findings (core-s1 bg|2, causal|2, contact|0, obj|1; core-s2 contact|0, obj|1; core-s3 contact|1, obj|0; router-s1 count|1, poss|0; router-s2 mirror|4, poss|1; router-s3 poss|2): mapped to MIRR-2, following the gemini-4-argon_v1-s2 precedent where the toothbrush vanishing from the hand while it stays visible in the mirror was labelled TP:MIRR-2. Different timestamp (09 vs 01).",
  "man-in-mirror reflection mismatches outside the 00:02-00:04 window (00:00.25, 01:75, 04:25, 09:00-09:75, and the frontal-vs-profile geometry claims): mapped to MIRR-1, following the precedents for argon 00:00, v1-s2 05-09 decoupling and v1-s2 geometric incompatibility.",
  "core-s2|man-in-mirror|character-continuity|1: the reflection head snaps from bowed to upright at 04.0-04.25 while the real head barely moves. Mapped to MIRR-1 as a reflection-vs-real mismatch. Its hairstyle-change component falls in the rejected hair micro-morph class.",
  "man-in-mirror 00:02-00:04 comb-vs-blade findings: these support both MIRR-1 and MIRR-2. Mapped to MIRR-1 when they focus on position/contact mismatch, and to MIRR-2 when they focus on the object changing kind or appearance (object-persistence, count-stability, possession-tracking roles).",
  "core-s3|phone|baseline-generalist|2, router-s1/s2/s3 text-stability text-morph claims (AZ-12 to AZ-X, header and status glyph drift, clock 4:41 to 4:49): mapped to PHON-1 garbled/unstable text, following the gemini-4-argon_v1-s3 08:00 text-morph precedent."
 ],
 "notes": "All red-bag-vanish findings on phone are FP (rejected class). router-s3|phone|environment-response|0 (bright band appears at ~01.0) is FP: frames show the phone tilting/panning at that moment, so the onset has a visible cause. man-in-mirror FPs: dry-shave/no-effect, looping, the head/hand snap at 04.0, hair restyling, and nonsensical forehead scraping (muse precedent). No Opus finding matched dancer-arm-flip-0002 or the phone-top-vanishes and mirror-brush-clips-face/face-morph EXTRA classes. Frames extracted to /tmp/opus55-adj/frames/g2/."
